# Engineering

Coding details: [`docs/conventions.md`](../../docs/conventions.md), and:

- [`.cursor/rules/csharp-tooling.mdc`](csharp-tooling.mdc)
- [`.cursor/rules/testing.mdc`](testing.mdc)

Human process: `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Local gate: `./build.ps1`.

## Layout

- Solution file: **`Graft.slnx`**. Do not commit `Graft.sln` (it is gitignored)
- Libraries stay split under `src/` (`Graft.Core`, `Graft.Protocol`, `Graft.Instrumentation`, `Graft.Instrumentation.Wpf`, `Graft.Instrumentation.Analyzer`, `Graft.McpServer`, `Graft.TestUtilities`). Do not collapse them into one project
- Tests stay under `tests/`. Sample apps stay under `tests/sample-apps/`
- `tools/Graft.SmokeClient` stays as the manual diagnostic client
- Canonical design is `docs/design.md`
- `.dev/task_*.md` are archived phase notes. Do not treat them as permission to code

## Targets

- Libraries default to `net8.0`. WPF projects use `net8.0-windows`
- Nullable is enabled. `TreatWarningsAsErrors` is false. StyleCop stays at warning severity
- Format with CSharpier (`dotnet csharpier`). Do not switch the gate to `dotnet format`
- Public API under `src/` needs XML docs (warning). See `csharp-tooling.mdc`
- Every Fact/Theory has `summary` and `remarks` with the headings Preconditions / Steps / Expected, written in English. See `testing.mdc`
- Comments and XML docs are English. See [`.cursor/skills/english-writing/SKILL.md`](../skills/english-writing/SKILL.md)

## Verification gate

- Windows, before a PR: `./build.ps1` (tool restore, CSharpier check, build `Graft.slnx`, unit tests that do not launch an app)
- Launched-app and SendInput tests are not part of that script. Run `dotnet test Graft.slnx -m:1`
- Hosted CI is `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Interactive UI CI is `.github/workflows/ui.yml` and stays opt-in
